<title>USA: Freddie Mac sees mid-teens earnings growth.</title>
<headline>Freddie Mac sees mid-teens earnings growth.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Freddie Mac officials said Thursday they are expecting a significant decline in credit losses through the end of the decade and earnings growth in the mid-teens over the next several years.</p>
<p>By the year 2000, credit losses as a percent of the total mortgage portfolio will be about half of the current level, according to the corporation's chief credit officer, Michael Stamper.</p>
